.TH LINUXCARE-MAINTENANCE 1 "August 2026" "LinuxCare 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linuxcare-maintenance \- internal scheduled-maintenance runner for LinuxCare
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linuxcare-maintenance
.B \-\-scheduled
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linuxcare-maintenance
runs LinuxCare's unprivileged scheduled maintenance workflow. It is intended to
be launched by LinuxCare-managed user-level systemd timers rather than invoked
interactively.
.PP
Scheduled maintenance does not silently perform privileged APT, Snap, Flatpak,
journal, firewall, SMART mutation, or package-removal operations.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-scheduled
Run the configured scheduled-maintenance workflow.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero on success and non-zero when configuration or maintenance execution
fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR linuxcare (1)
.SH AUTHOR
MilMit <info@milmit.net>
